-- title:
--   Branch ideals of the crossing model UV=π^E
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring, let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $E$ be a natural number with $1 \le E$. Work in the crossing model $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ (\pi^{E})$, that is, the quotient of the two-variable formal power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\ (\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\pi^{E})$, and write $c$ for `const (π ^ E) π`, the class of the constant series $\pi$, and $u$, $v$ for the two coordinate elements `U (π ^ E)`, `V (π ^ E)` of this ring. The conclusion is the conjunction of five assertions: the two ideals $(c,u)$ and $(c,v)$ meet in the principal ideal $(c)$; for every natural number $n$ one has $v^{n} \notin (c,u)$; for every natural number $n$ one has $u^{n} \notin (c,v)$ (in particular, taking $n = 0$, both ideals are proper); the infimum over all $n$ of $(c,u) + (v^{n})$ equals $(c,u)$; and the infimum over all $n$ of $(c,v) + (u^{n})$ equals $(c,v)$.
--
--   These are the basic properties of the two branch ideals of the local crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$: they cut out the two branches through the node, intersect in the ideal of the uniformiser, and are closed under adding higher powers of the transverse coordinate. They are used in the identification of the kernels of the two residue maps of a node ring with the branch ideals, in the rigidity statement that an automorphism of the model fixing the constant $\pi$ and not sending $U$ into the second branch ideal multiplies $V$ by a unit, and in the construction of crossing presentations of node rings of modular curves at supersingular crossings of the special fibre.
